# Operating TOOL

The single source of truth for driving TOOL. TOOL runs AI-free: a human double-clicks a
`.command` and edits a `.config.jsonc`. This skill just maps a request to the right command and
knobs. See 08-skills-and-ai-integration.md.

## When this applies

Any request to <list the kinds of jobs TOOL handles>. If the request is something TOOL does not
do, this skill does not apply.

## The commands

| Job | Command | Key config knobs |
|---|---|---|
| <job A> | `commands/do-a.command` | `PROMPT`, `SEED`, `OUT_DIR` |
| <job B> | `commands/do-b.command` | `PROMPT`, `WIDTH`, `HEIGHT`, `SEED` |

## How to run

- Double-click the `.command`, or run it headless: `./commands/do-a.command` (edit the config
  first, or pass `KEY=VALUE` overrides if the launcher supports them).
- Or call the engine directly: `.venv/bin/TOOL SUBCOMMAND "PROMPT" --seed 7`.

## Rules

1. Always set `SEED` for reproducibility. Same config plus same seed yields identical output.
2. Output and `provenance.json` land in `out/<name>/<timestamp>/`. Never overwrite.
3. If a run fails, read the printed error and check the paths in the `.config.jsonc`.
4. Do not require any AI at runtime. The tool must work for a human with just the command.
